---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Notice from "../components/ui/Notice.astro";
import { SITE, CONTACT, LEGAL_UPDATED } from "../consts";
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`Terms of use for ${SITE.name}.`}
  lede={`Last updated ${LEGAL_UPDATED}.`}
>
  <Notice title="Read this first">
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is an independent, experimental project run by one individual. It is
      not a company or a commercial service, nothing is sold, and it is provided as is
      and as available. Data may be lost or reset at any time.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Do not upload confidential, regulated, or personal data, and do not depend on
        it for anything that matters.
      </strong>
    </p>
  </Notice>

  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you and the individual maintainer of {
      SITE.name
    } ("the maintainer", "we", "us") and cover your use of this website and the {
      SITE.name
    } application (together, "the Project"). If you do not accept them, do not use
    the Project.
  </p>

  <h2>Eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of majority where you live, and
    legally able to enter into this agreement. Do not use the Project if you are
    barred from doing so under any applicable law or sanctions programme.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You need an account to use the Project. Keep your credentials secure, provide
    accurate information, and take responsibility for everything done under your
    account. Accounts are for your own use and must not be shared or resold.
  </p>

  <h2>What you own, and what you are responsible for</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>You own your content.</strong> You keep all rights to the data you upload
    and to any dataset, adapter, model, or output you produce with the Project. The
    maintainer claims <strong>no ownership</strong> of, and asserts <strong>
      no licence over
    </strong>, your data, your trained models, or their outputs, beyond the limited,
    temporary permission needed to store and process them so the Project can run for
    you. That permission ends when you delete the content or your account.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>You are solely responsible for that content and its consequences.</strong>
    That includes confirming that:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      you have the legal right to upload and process every piece of data you submit,
      including any consent, confidentiality, contractual, or data-protection
      obligation attached to it;
    </li>
    <li>
      your use complies with the licence of every base model you fine-tune, and with
      the terms of any third-party model provider you route requests to;
    </li>
    <li>
      anything you build, deploy, publish, or rely on from the Project is lawful and
      suitable for the purpose you put it to.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The maintainer does not review, moderate, endorse, or verify what users upload or
    produce, and is not responsible for it.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not use the Project to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break any law, or infringe anyone's intellectual property, privacy, or other rights;</li>
    <li>upload content you have no right to use, or data about people who have not consented;</li>
    <li>
      process special-category, health, financial, biometric, government-identifier,
      or other regulated personal data;
    </li>
    <li>
      build or run models intended to harass, defraud, deceive, surveil, or harm
      people, or to generate illegal material, including sexual content involving
      minors;
    </li>
    <li>
      generate or automate advice presented as professional legal, medical,
      financial, or safety guidance;
    </li>
    <li>
      attempt to breach isolation between accounts, access data that is not yours,
      probe or disrupt the infrastructure, mine cryptocurrency, or circumvent usage
      limits;
    </li>
    <li>redistribute or resell the Project as your own service.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Access may be suspended or removed immediately, without notice, for any use that
    appears to breach this section.
  </p>

  <h2>Model output</h2>
  <p>
    Language models produce output that can be inaccurate, biased, offensive,
    infringing, or entirely fabricated. Evaluation tooling is provided to help you
    measure quality, but the Project makes <strong>no representation</strong> about
    the correctness, originality, legality, or fitness of any output. Output is not
    professional advice of any kind. Any decision you take using it is yours alone,
    and meaningful consequences require your own human review.
  </p>

  <h2>No charges, and third-party provider costs</h2>
  <p>
    The Project sells nothing and adds no margin or fee of its own. You can use the
    default model endpoints or configure your own provider API key. Where a
    third-party model provider is involved, whatever that provider charges for its
    own usage is a matter strictly between you and that provider, on their terms and
    at their rates. The maintainer is not a party to that relationship and is not
    liable for costs you incur with any third party.
  </p>
  <p>
    Compute is finite, so runs may be rate-limited, queued, or capped to keep the
    environment usable.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability, data loss, and security</h2>
  <p>
    The Project is experimental and may change, break, lose data, or shut down
    permanently at any time, without notice or liability. There is no service level,
    no backup guarantee, and no commitment to retain anything you store.
    <strong>Keep your own copy of anything you care about.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Reasonable technical measures are used (encryption in transit, authentication,
    encryption at rest for stored provider credentials), but <strong>
      no system is secure and no assurance against compromise, unauthorised access,
      or data exposure is given or implied.
    </strong> By using the Project you accept that risk. If you discover a
    vulnerability, please email us rather than disclosing it publicly.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Project is provided "as is" and "as
    available", without warranties or conditions of any kind, whether express,
    implied, or statutory — including any implied warranty of merchantability,
    fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, quiet enjoyment, or
    non-infringement.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, and taking into account that the Project
    is supplied free of charge as an experimental, non-commercial undertaking,
    neither the maintainer nor any contributor is liable for any indirect,
    incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, nor for any
    loss of profits, revenue, goodwill, business, data, or models, arising out of or
    relating to the Project — even if advised of the possibility.
  </p>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, total aggregate liability for all claims
    relating to the Project is limited to <strong>
      the greater of the amount you paid to use it (which is zero) or USD 50
    </strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion of certain warranties or
    liabilities. Where that applies, the exclusions above apply only to the extent
    permitted, and nothing here limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Indemnity</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the maintainer and any
    contributor from and against any claim, demand, proceeding, loss, liability,
    damage, cost, or expense (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of or
    relating to: the data or content you upload; the models or outputs you produce,
    deploy, or distribute; your breach of these terms or of any applicable law; or
    any third-party right you infringe through your use of the Project.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting infringement or misuse</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe content processed through the Project infringes your rights or
    otherwise breaks these terms, email us with enough detail to identify it and it
    will be reviewed and removed where appropriate.
  </p>

  <h2>Suspension, termination, and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    You may stop using the Project at any time and request deletion of your account
    and data. Access may be suspended or terminated at any time, with or without
    cause or notice, including to protect the Project or other users, or if the
    Project is discontinued. On termination, hosted artifacts become inaccessible —
    export anything you want to keep beforehand.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may be updated at any time. The date above reflects the current
    version; there is no notification mechanism, so review this page before relying
    on anything here. Continuing to use the Project after a change means you accept
    the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws applicable at the maintainer's place of
    residence, without regard to conflict-of-law rules, and any dispute is subject to
    the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts competent for that place. Before
    starting any formal proceeding, you agree to contact us by email and attempt to
    resolve the matter informally.
  </p>

  <h2>General</h2>
  <p>
    If any provision is held unenforceable, the remainder stays in force. A failure
    to enforce a provision is not a waiver of it. You may not assign these terms; the
    maintainer may assign them to any successor of the Project. These terms, together
    with the <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>, are the entire agreement between
    you and the maintainer regarding the Project, and supersede any prior
    understanding. Nothing here creates a partnership, agency, employment, or joint
    venture between us.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.admin}`}>{CONTACT.admin}</a>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
